{"kft": [{"id": "kft", "headword": "कृत्", "headword_slp1": "kft", "fold": "kft", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "1 कृत् कृन्त॑ति कृन्त॑˚ते (कर्तति), pp. कृत्त॑ cut,\ncut off, cleave, split, divide, destroy. C. कर्तयति (कृन्तयति)\nthe same. — अप & अपि cut off. अव cut off, destroy. C. cause to be\ngashed. उद् cut out or off, carve, tear asunder, destroy. नि cut or\nhew down, cut or tear off;\n M. cut one's self (e.g. the nails). C. cause\nto be cut. परि cut round, clip, cut off, exclude from (abl.). प्र\ncut off or asunder. वि the same, tear to pieces, lacerate, destroy. C.\nthe same. सम् cut etc. (together).", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "2 कृत् कृण॑त्ति twist the thread, spin. C. क्र्तयति weave.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "3 कृत् a. making, doing, causing, effecting;\n maker, performer,\nauthor of (—˚) m. a suffix forming nouns from roots, also = कृदन्त\nm.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "kfta": [{"id": "kfta", "headword": "कृत", "headword_slp1": "kfta", "fold": "kfta", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "कृत॑ a. made, done, prepared, arranged, appointed, got;\npresent, ready, fit, proper, good. Often ˚— having done, doing using,\nshowing, betraying etc. —n. it is done, i.e. shall be done instantly;\nw. instr. (±सह) be it done with, i.e. away with, enough of! n. as\nsubst. act, deed, work, esp. religious work, sacrifice, ceremony, etc.;\nservice, benefit;\n stake at game;\n booty in battle;\n the (lucky) Four-side\nof the die;\n the first or golden age. कृतेन because or instead of\n(gen. or —˚);\n कृते the same. abs. for something.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["कृतं"], "synonyms_slp1": ["kftaM"]}, {"id": "kftA", "headword": "कृता", "headword_slp1": "kftA", "fold": "kfta", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "कृ॑ता f. cleft, abyss.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "kftaka": [{"id": "kf